-- ownership: a lambda applied directly to a function parameter hands that
-- parameter back to itself. v1 once recursed through `passOn` without end
-- and overflowed the stack (#1747); it now stops the re-entry. The summary
-- is pessimistic (`unseen`, `borrowed`), never a crash and never an accept
-- of more than the parameter's calls can justify.
applyTwice f x = (λg y → g (g y)) f x
